Despite some of these caveats, our data support the conten-
tion that EPT is associated with dysfunctional activation pre-
dominantly within the dentato–rubro–olivary pathway. Our
study therefore demonstrates the ability of functional MRI to
detect subtle changes associated with pathological dysactiva-
tion even within brainstem structures.
